DTSTART:20261021T220000Z
DTEND:20261022T014000Z
DESCRIPTION:The hot-line suspense comedy from Stanley Kubrick.\n\nWhen a rogue U.S. general orders an unauthorized nuclear attack on the Soviet Union\, leaders in the War Room race to prevent a global catastrophe. \n\nPartnering with the Philosophy\, Political Science\, and Economics Student Group\, the ASLC presents a hysterically enlightening screening of Dr. Strangelove or: How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Love the Bomb (1964). Professor Mark Souva will be giving a brief introduction before the screening and will remain afterwards to answer any questions. \n\nDoors: 6PM\nShow: 7PM\nRuntime: 1h35m\n---\nEvent Details: https://hq.fsu.edu/rsvp?id=377582
GEO:30.440947;-84.299528
LOCATION:Askew Student Life Center
SUMMARY:Dr. Strangelove or: How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Love the Bomb (1964) Film Screening
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/dr-strangelove-or-how-i-learned-to-stop-worrying-and-love-the-bomb-1964-film-screening
END:VEVENT
